# Zero-Clone — indexed remote only

## Product law

Coop works **without downloading a local copy** of any repo. Repository intelligence
(chat, quick actions, slash commands, agent tools, Blast, Gaps, Trace, Owner,
Understand Repo) must use **indexed remote evidence + on-demand codehost fetches**.

**Never** scan open VS Code folders, local clones, or `workspaceFolders` for
callers, file bodies, or “verified” dependents and present that as remote success.

## Canonical sources

| Need | Source |
|---|---|
| File body | `IndexedRepoWorkspace.readFile` → API / codehost only |
| Inventory / tree | Indexed `repo_stats` / graph (via `IndexedRepoWorkspace`) |
| Dependents / Blast | Durable import graph / SCIP / Zoekt — never `workspace` disk walk |
| Search | Cloud index / Zoekt — never local `findFiles` for answer gather |

Policy flag: `src/workspace/zeroClonePolicy.ts` (`mayReadLocalRepoDiskForIntelligence`).

## Banned

| Reject | Prefer |
|---|---|
| `readWorkspaceFileFromDisk` / `readLocalWorkspaceFiles` on gather | Remote fetch |
| Preferring local clone in `IndexedRepoWorkspace.readFile` | Codehost / `fetchRepoFile` |
| Blast `localRoots` / `source: "workspace"` as a remote win | `import-parse` / `scip` / `zoekt` |
| Offline “analyze from local workspace” fallbacks for Use-repo | Cached remote or unavailable |
| Agent `read_file` resolving workspace absolute paths first | Remote reader first/only |

## Allowed exceptions (not repo intelligence)

- Patch apply into an open editor buffer
- AGENTS.md / prompt library pickers
- Autocomplete on the active buffer
- Explicit `fileSource: "external"` uploads (Cmd+O outside the Use-repo)

## Self-check

Before shipping gather/quick-action changes: if the user has Coop-AI open locally
and Use-repo is `plane`, could any path still answer from Coop-AI’s disk? If yes, fail.
